Package: spatialDWLS
Title: Cell Type Deconvolution of Spatial Transcriptomics with Dampened Weighted Least Squares
Version: 0.1.1
Authors@R: c(
    person("Rui", "Dong", role = "aut",
        comment = "original spatialDWLS method and implementation"),
    person("Guo-Cheng", "Yuan", email = "guo-cheng.yuan@mssm.edu",
        role = "aut"),
    person("Ruben", "Dries", email = "rubendries@gmail.com",
        role = c("aut", "cre"), comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-7650-7754")),
    person("Jiaji", "George Chen", email = "jiajic@bu.edu", role = "ctb",
        comment = "package and website")
    )
Description: Estimates the cell type composition of each spot of a spatial
    transcriptomics experiment from a single-cell reference, following
    spatialDWLS (Dong and Yuan 2021, <doi:10.1186/s13059-021-02362-7>), which
    builds on dampened weighted least squares (DWLS; Tsoucas et al. 2019,
    <doi:10.1038/s41467-019-10802-z>). Spots are solved in two rounds:
    candidate cell types are chosen per cluster by enrichment, then each spot
    is re-solved against the types present in it. Works on dense or sparse
    matrices, in parallel through 'BiocParallel', and over windows of spots
    for expression stores that do not fit in memory.
